{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Selah</b> — from the root of מסלה. And likewise: \"Gath [of] the winepress of YHWH\" — from the root of דרך. Only \"Selah\" is a different root:" "<b>Gath</b> — winepress:" "<b>Virgin of</b> — construct state attached to בת. And 'daughter of Judah' — the entire tribe; and 'the virgin' — Jerusalem:"], :book :lamentations, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "The Hebrew quotes גת דרך ה׳ allude to Isaiah 63:3 (גת without vav); Ibn Ezra plays on dual senses. Reading left as Hebrew script per voice rules."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Lamentations -- Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%9E%D7%92%D7%99%D7%9C%D7%AA_%D7%90%D7%99%D7%9B%D7%94"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:07:45.989771945Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}